obuglennyy-dnevnik-name = charred diary
obuglennyy-dnevnik-desc = A little book with burned edges, reeking unbearably of sulfur, saltpeter, and singed hair. The pages are brittle as dried autumn leaves. The author's elegant, ornate handwriting begins to twitch toward the end of the entry, the letters jumping, the pressure growing so fierce that the quill tore through the paper in places.
obuglennyy-dnevnik-content = [color=#4b0082]Fools. Pitiful, worthless dilettantes.


    {"Academics sit their robes threadbare for years studying the conjuring of little water, the levitation of feathers, or, All-Father forgive us, [italic]healing[/italic]. They have turned magic into a convenient tool for commoners! But magic is not a trade. Magic is the manifestation of absolute superiority!"}


    {"True beauty is fleet1ng. 1t must bl1nd! Deafen! Leave behind only scorched earth and sacred awe in the hearts of those fortunate enough to survive!"}


    {"My so-called c0lleagues laugh at me. They say knowing only 0ne spell is a disgrace. But why would I need an arsenal of cheap tricks when I have grasped the ABS0LUTE?! Why waste mana on wretched little fireballs?!"}


    {"[bold][color=#ff4500]ART 1S AN EXPL0SION![/color][/bold]"}


    {"0 crimson-black flame sleeping in the abyss! Lord of ash and master of ruins! I call upon your true might! Reject the laws of this world, tear apart the chains of creation, and reveal your punishing hand!"}


    {"Tremble, wretched g0blins, for now you shall witness my symphony of destructi0n!"}


    {"[bold][color=#ff0000]E X P L 0 0 0 0 0[/color][/bold]▓▓▓▓▓▓▒▒▒▒▒░░░░....."}


    {"[color=#8b0000]`~``~`~~~`~~~``~[/color]"}

    {"...m... mana... ran 0ut... carry... mwe... ░░░[/color]"}

butylka-strannogo-vina-name = bottle of strange wine
butylka-strannogo-vina-desc = A bottle of dark glass covered in dust. The cork sits tight, too tight, as though it had been hammered in. The label has worn down to a gray smudge. Only a couple of letters can be made out: "W..." and "...ne". Whether it holds wine, vinegar, or poison will be known only to the one who opens it.

pokrytyy-ryaskoy-pergament-name = duckweed-covered parchment
pokrytyy-ryaskoy-pergament-desc = A damp, crumpled piece of parchment thickly smeared with dried swamp mud. The smell is enough to make the eyes water, carrying rotten eggs, decay, and stagnant water. The text has run in places from the moisture.
pokrytyy-ryaskoy-pergament-content = [head=3]The Cursed Marshes[/head]

    {"[italic]"}

    {"A local fool promised us silver and more,"}

    {"Said the marshes were bursting with treasure in store."}

    {"So light on our feet, through the mire we went,"}

    {"Dreaming of purses grown fat and well-spent."}


    {"But when to our chests in the bog we sank down,"}

    {"We knew that the marsh meant to see us all drown."}

    {"From murky black water where dead rushes sleep,"}

    {"The [color=#2e8b57]drowned ones[/color] came crawling from silence and deep."}


    {"Our chieftain swung hard with his axe in the gloom,"}

    {"But the quarrel was ended with one wet doom:"}

    {"A [color=#556b2f]water hag[/color] dragged him below,"}

    {"And stuffed his mouth shut with green weeds from the flow."}


    {"I dropped my pike and crawled over moss,"}

    {"And nearly died choking on foul swamp gas."}

    {"Now I sit by the fire, still shaking and sore,"}

    {"[bold]No bog in this world shall take me once more![/bold]"}

    {"[/italic]"}

razbuhshiy-zhurnal-name = swollen journal
razbuhshiy-zhurnal-desc = A thick leather-bound book badly damaged by damp. The pages have warped into waves, gray mold spots them in places, and the entries are written in a tight, irritated hand.
razbuhshiy-zhurnal-content = [head=3]Defense Journal of the Rebel Fortress[/head]


    {"[italic]Day Thirty-Two. Garrison Commander Vsevolod Temnov.[/italic]"}


    {"I hasten to record for history: the siege is lifted. The pirates have gone back where they came from. And no, there were no heroic sorties or epic battles upon the walls for capital bards to turn into false ballads. The captain of those halfwits simply realized that storming a heap of moldy stone in the middle of a bog is a deeply unprofitable occupation. Especially when your band dies of dysentery and swamp fever faster than from crossbow bolts."}


    {"The siege is lifted. We endured. The fortress was not surrendered. It sounds proud enough, provided one does not look around."}


    {"The roof of the old arsenal finally collapsed from damp tonight, turning a good half of our powder into useless mud. A third of the garrison is vomiting farther than it can see and lying in the infirmary with fever. There is almost nothing to eat, and the well water tastes of slime and iron. We held this scrap of swamp, but unless the quartermasters at headquarters deign to send carts with food, medicine, and dry footwraps in the next few days, the pirates will not even need to come back."}


    {"Tomorrow morning I will send a messenger raven to command. Let them send supplies, or we shall perish here of ordinary damp and pride in the ruins we held."}

zaplesnevelyy-pergament-name = moldy parchment
zaplesnevelyy-pergament-desc = A rough sheet of paper pinned to a wooden beam with a dagger. The text is full of biting remarks and heavily underlined lines.
zaplesnevelyy-pergament-content = [head=3]Order for the Rebel Fortress Garrison[/head]


    {"[italic]From Commander Temnov.[/italic]"}


    {"For those idiots who decided that the pirates leaving is a reason to open the emergency ale stores, let me explain. We did not win. We simply proved more stubborn and more accustomed to the local filth than those sea rats."}


    {"[bold]I order the following:[/bold]"}

    {"- Boil the well water twice. Anyone who gulps it raw will be flogged by my personal order, so I do not have to waste bandages and the healer's time on him later."}

    {"- Gather the bodies abandoned beyond the walls, pour oil over them, and burn them to all the hells. The swamp already stinks of rot. We do not need corpse poison sitting under our very gates."}

    {"- Double the watches. Just because they abandoned their rotten ladders does not mean two or three especially stupid looters will not try to come back for forgotten junk."}


    {"And for the sake of all the gods, stop roaring your victory hymns in the yard. They give me a migraine. Anyone wishing to demonstrate an excess of strength and joy may go clean the latrine pits at once. Dismissed."}

gryaznyy-pergament-name = dirty parchment
gryaznyy-pergament-desc = A scrap of thick, yellowed parchment. Its edges are frayed, and the whole surface shows dried brown stains and marks from dirty fingers. The text is written in clumsy, oversized letters that either crawl over one another or barely fit on the line.
gryaznyy-pergament-content = [color=#4a3627]Yest'day, see, we set out with the wagon train. Me, I'm a trading man, not some fool. Hired guards. One... man joined up. Gloomy as an owl. All in black iron, one eye gone, and instead of a left hand some iron thing. And that sword... Mother of God! That weren't no sword, that was a raw lump of iron! By the saints, how he drags that beast about, may I burst if I know?!

    {"So we ride, see, ride along. Then bam! Thieves jump from the bushes. Spears out, faces mean, shouting: \"Drop yer breeches, merchant, hand over the goods!\" I dive under the cart in fright. Sit there shaking like an aspen leaf, praying they leave me my life at least."}

    {"And that black one... He pulls out that cart-pole of his! And roars!"}
    {"And then he starts on them... holy saints..."}

    {"[bold][color=#8b0000]CRACK![/color][/bold]"}

    {"He cuts them in half! Right through their mail, like rotten turnips! [color=#8b0000]▓▓▓▒░[/color] Blood spraying every which way, splashed right on my mug! Arms and legs flying, guts all over the road... One thief tried coming from the side, so he grabbed him by the throat with that iron stump and [italic]crunch![/italic]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000]▓▓▓▓▒▒░░[/color] Splattered all my grain sacks, damn him!"}

    {"Finished every last one. Stands in the middle of the road, soaked in blood, breathing heavy like a forge bellows. Throws the sword over his shoulder. Looks at me from under his brow with that one eye... and I confess, I near filled my breeches, pardon the word. Thought he'd chop me into cabbage next. But he just spat and rasped:"}
    {"[italic]\"Why are you standing there? We ride.\"[/italic]"}

    {"So we ride. Goods are safe, glory to the gods. But now I sit on the driver's bench afraid to turn my back on him. Hell knows if that is a man at all, curse him sideways...[/color]"}

