accuratnoe-pismo-name = neat letter
accuratnoe-pismo-desc = A surprisingly well-preserved letter written in a careful hand.
accuratnoe-pismo-content = Keri,

    {"Once more I am beside our tree. Its crown murmurs dully today, as though whispering with the shadows of the swamp, and a silver glow shows through the bark, exactly like your eyes on the evening when we planted this sapling among the black mosses. The winds of the four elements bring me the voices of spirits, yet none of them can say the one thing that matters: when you will return. I have listened to them for eighty years, and still I come here with parchment."}

    {"Do not worry for your castle. I visit it whenever the mists allow passage through the bogs without harm to the uninvited. Your wards remain whole, and the darkness you bridled sleeps evenly in the dungeons, like a tamed beast. I merely mend the protective contour above the library and brush dust from the grimoires, so that magic remembers the warmth of your palms. You always said dark art was not villainy, but reins holding the abyss back from the unworthy. I remember. And I am proud of your burden, though it parted us."}

    {"I know that now, beyond the veil of the dense worlds, you speak with Morbius, trying to bargain forgiveness for simple mortals and preserve the island he threatens to swallow into oblivion. You, my brightest shadow, always cared for innocent souls, even when all the light called you the hermit of the wicked marshes. I spoke with the spirit of the old abbot from Magnus's mountain skete. He said that each of your steps in the astral leaves behind a shimmering thread, like a vow. Then truth is on your side."}

    {"I write this letter not to reproach you for absence. Only so that you, there in timelessness, may stretch forth a shadow and read it in the roots of the tree that bound us more tightly than any prayer. My elemental magic still feeds it, and every leaf keeps a part of yours. I am growing old, Keri, but I will not tire of waiting. Return when you have finished speaking with eternity itself. I will meet you at the castle gates with the same damp wind that carried your scent through the astral all these long years."}

    {"Forever yours,"}
    {"Goldur the Wise"}

